C09 review round 2 negative regression probes: the issuer-coverage contract
(closed CRL issuer population) ran against the pre-fix matcher. Two phases:

Phase 1 - first red: the new regression TestMTLSRejectsIssuersWithoutRevocationCoverage
ran against the committed pre-fix source (d1eebc79bc24455b6f1907e3b343c8effc255800)
which still accepted uncovered issuers:

--- FAIL: TestMTLSRejectsIssuersWithoutRevocationCoverage (5.05s)
    mtls_test.go:618: timeout waiting for issuer-without-coverage denial: states=4 identities=2 receipts=2 failures=[]

The secondary-issued (uncovered) colliding collector authenticated and INGESTED
(identities=2 receipts=2, zero denials): exactly the review finding.

Phase 2 - reverted experiment: after implementing the fix, internal/pki/identity.go
was temporarily reverted to the d1eebc7 matcher in the worktree only, and both
contract-bearing tests ran against it:

--- FAIL: TestMTLSTypedVerdictsUseRealHandshakeTranscripts (5.03s)
    mtls_test.go:494: timeout waiting for CA2 chain denial: states=1 identities=1 receipts=0 failures=[]
--- FAIL: TestMTLSRejectsIssuersWithoutRevocationCoverage (5.05s)
    mtls_test.go:622: timeout waiting for issuer-without-coverage denial: states=4 identities=2 receipts=2 failures=[]
FAIL    github.com/Parsa-Emami/Miragemesh/tests 10.090s

The CA2 chain was captured (accepted) instead of denied under the old matcher and
the colliding collector ingested. Result: both regressions fail under the old
(coverage-blind) matcher and pass under the committed fix; identity.go was
restored before the verification battery. Not a tool run against the delivered
source; kept outside main commands.
